    "### Hugging Face Open LLM Leaderboard — EDA\n",
    "\n",
    "The Epoch AI analysis above provides supporting evidence on the training cost side of scaling — it establishes that larger models require substantially more compute to train. Here, the Hugging Face Open LLM Leaderboard directly addresses our main hypothesis: do performance gains on standardized benchmarks exhibit diminishing returns in inference cost as model scale increases?\n",
    "\n",
    "The five figures below use 4,456 models from the cleaned leaderboard dataset, connecting benchmark performance (`average_score`), inference CO₂ cost (`co2_cost`), and model size (`parameters`). They build progressively toward a concrete answer at the 70B parameter boundary."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Valid models: 4,456\n",
      "Models <=70B: 4,310  |  >70B: 146\n",
      "\n",
      "Avg score range: 0.74 – 52.08\n",
      "CO₂ cost range:  0.064 – 186.61 kg\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "from scipy.stats import mannwhitneyu, binned_statistic\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_palette('tab10')\n",
    "\n",
    "HF_PATH = \"data/02-processed/hf_parameters_co2.ndjson\"\n",
    "raw_hf = pd.read_json(HF_PATH, lines=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only the flat columns needed for these EDA plots\n",
    "hf_eda = raw_hf[['model', 'average_score', 'co2_cost', 'parameters', 'precision']].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Filter to valid positive values\n",
    "hf_eda = hf_eda[\n",
    "    (hf_eda['parameters'] > 0) &\n",
    "    (hf_eda['co2_cost'] > 0) &\n",
    "    hf_eda['average_score'].notna()\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Log-scale transformations\n",
    "hf_eda['log10_params'] = np.log10(hf_eda['parameters'])\n",
    "hf_eda['log10_co2']    = np.log10(hf_eda['co2_cost'])\n",
    "hf_eda['log1p_co2']    = np.log1p(hf_eda['co2_cost'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Efficiency metric: benchmark score per log-unit of inference CO2\n",
    "hf_eda['perf_efficiency'] = hf_eda['average_score'] / hf_eda['log1p_co2'].replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 70B threshold grouping (the boundary our hypothesis specifically tests)\n",
    "THRESH_70B = 7e10\n",
    "hf_eda['grp'] = np.where(hf_eda['parameters'] <= THRESH_70B, '<=70B', '>70B')\n",
    "\n",
