   "source": [
    "**Interpretation.** The slope on `log_params` can be interpreted as an elasticity: it describes the expected change in log training compute for a one-unit increase in log parameter count. In our sample of 815 models with non-missing compute, the fitted slope is 1.724 and the model explains 76.6% of the variation in log training FLOPs (R² = 0.766). A strong fit supports the idea that parameter count is a meaningful proxy for training compute *within the subset that reports compute*. Because many models are missing compute values, this estimate should be interpreted as conditional on the reported-compute subset rather than a guarantee for all models in the full Epoch database."
